      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Writing all terms as powers of \\(2,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac{8^{10}+4^{10}}{8^4+4^{11}} &=\\frac{2^{30}+2^{20}}{2^{12}+2^{22}}\\\\ &=\\frac{2^{20}(2^{10}+1)} {2^{12}(1+2^{10})}\\\\ &=2^8. \\end{aligned} \\] Its positive square root is \\(2^4=16.\\) Thus the correct answer is B.",
